WEBVTT

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:02.260
GA...

00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:06.080
Is about to staaaart.

00:00:16.490 --> 00:00:21.460
Geijutsuka Art Design Class

00:01:46.380 --> 00:01:47.320
Good morning!

00:01:47.830 --> 00:01:49.420
Noda-chan, your hair, your hair!

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:50.220
Hmm?

00:01:51.630 --> 00:01:52.750
Nooo!

00:01:52.750 --> 00:01:54.220
Wow. That was rough.

00:01:54.220 --> 00:01:56.730
Looks like everyone struggled 
through the strong wind.

00:01:56.730 --> 00:01:58.410
Noda, since you're so small,

00:01:58.410 --> 00:02:01.400
we were talking about how 
maybe you'd been blown away.

00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:03.230
Oh, well it was a close call.

00:02:04.370 --> 00:02:07.760
But since Namiko-san was 
there, I was saved.

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:10.070
Noda, sit here for a second.

00:02:10.070 --> 00:02:11.110
I have something to tell you.

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:16.990
Namiko-san messed up my hair!

00:02:17.590 --> 00:02:20.910
Namiko-dono, the button on your 
right sleeve is coming detached.

00:02:21.950 --> 00:02:24.760
Oh! Masa, you carry 
around a sewing set?

00:02:25.430 --> 00:02:28.030
Hmm? Did I get something in my eyes?

00:02:28.030 --> 00:02:28.560
Here.

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:31.260
Oh! Eye drops. Thanks, Kyouju.

00:02:31.260 --> 00:02:32.350
You're amazing.

00:02:32.350 --> 00:02:33.210
As expected!

00:02:36.430 --> 00:02:39.500
<b>Strong Wind Stories</b>

00:02:49.590 --> 00:02:52.310
Good morning. 
The wind is crazy today.

00:02:52.310 --> 00:02:55.250
Mezamashi TV was saying that there 
would be rain this afternoon, too!

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:10.270
<b>Grrrrr</b>

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:11.270
<b>Thump</b>

00:03:10.990 --> 00:03:12.390
Hurry up already, you idiot.

00:03:12.390 --> 00:03:13.430
You're in my way.

00:03:21.330 --> 00:03:23.110
I made it somehow...

00:03:25.090 --> 00:03:28.070
I'll just rest a little bit before 
I go to the nurse's office.

00:03:30.770 --> 00:03:32.460
Oh, good morning.

00:03:32.460 --> 00:03:34.260
The wind is really 
something this morning.

00:03:34.260 --> 00:03:35.910
Good morning, Buchi-san.

00:03:35.910 --> 00:03:37.590
This morning is the worst.

00:03:37.590 --> 00:03:39.750
Oh my, what happened, Aa-san?

00:03:40.030 --> 00:03:41.870
That's quite an interesting pose.

00:03:42.260 --> 00:03:45.640
I don't really know, but she's 
been like this the whole time...

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:47.140
Pupuppidoo

00:03:47.980 --> 00:03:49.970
What? “Pupuppidoo”?

00:03:49.970 --> 00:03:52.350
Ohh, yes, yes. 
I see what you mean.

00:03:56.080 --> 00:03:58.020
Hey, what happened to you, Uozumi?

00:03:58.020 --> 00:04:00.190
You're bandaged up like a cartoon.

00:04:00.190 --> 00:04:03.740
I said I didn't see them, 
but I still got beat up.

00:04:03.740 --> 00:04:05.500
Women sure are scary.

00:04:07.530 --> 00:04:10.570
Hey, Kisaragi, since when 
did you have color inks?

00:04:10.570 --> 00:04:12.290
Oh, you mean these?

00:04:12.290 --> 00:04:16.030
This is actually a present 
that my friend in GA 3

00:04:16.030 --> 00:04:19.690
got me when I passed the 
entrance exams here.

00:04:19.690 --> 00:04:21.540
Oh, the person you talked 
about before, right?

00:04:21.540 --> 00:04:24.750
Wow! This is a famous 
brand of color ink!

00:04:24.750 --> 00:04:25.910
Awesome!

00:04:25.910 --> 00:04:26.890
Yes!

00:04:26.890 --> 00:04:29.370
I always had this notion, 
since I was a kid,

00:04:29.370 --> 00:04:32.160
that color ink was a grown-up 
artist's material.

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:34.460
I was so happy!

00:04:34.460 --> 00:04:38.140
I had planned on using it as soon 
as I got into high school, but...

00:04:38.940 --> 00:04:39.760
But?

00:04:40.040 --> 00:04:40.790
<b>Thunk</b>

00:04:40.730 --> 00:04:41.800
<i>Mumble mumble mumble...</i>

00:04:41.800 --> 00:04:42.720
What?

00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:45.640
When you try to use them, suddenly 
they seem too valuable to open?

00:04:45.640 --> 00:04:47.680
What are you, an elementary schooler?!

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:49.270
Art Room 1

00:04:49.270 --> 00:04:51.050
Hey, hey, Buchi-sanya?

00:04:49.280 --> 00:05:12.390
Sketch sketch

00:04:51.050 --> 00:04:52.640
What is it, Aa-sanya?

00:04:52.640 --> 00:04:55.740
We have to go get paint 
to color this with.

00:04:55.740 --> 00:04:58.200
But it's such a hassle to 
get it from my locker...

00:04:58.200 --> 00:05:00.980
In that case, you'd 
have to use ESP.

00:05:00.980 --> 00:05:01.970
I see.

00:05:01.970 --> 00:05:05.190
All right! Poster paint, come!

00:05:08.420 --> 00:05:10.370
Like that was going to work.

00:05:10.370 --> 00:05:12.390
Yup. I'll go get it.

00:05:13.340 --> 00:05:17.990
It was tough to get to class, but 
coming back is easy with a tailwind.

00:05:17.990 --> 00:05:20.400
Look! If I do this...

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:22.030
It's even easier!

00:05:22.780 --> 00:05:24.500
They are working clothes, after all.

00:05:24.500 --> 00:05:26.800
Oh, I should've worn one, too.

00:05:26.800 --> 00:05:27.600
I wonder how fa- Huh?

00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:31.440
Kisaragi! That only happens in stories!

00:05:31.440 --> 00:05:32.780
Big sis, now's your time!

00:05:32.780 --> 00:05:34.680
What are you telling me for?!

00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:39.960
Wow. The wind hasn't 
died down at all!

00:05:39.960 --> 00:05:41.120
My bangs are all a mess.

00:05:41.340 --> 00:05:43.800
Could this be an off-season typhoon?

00:05:43.800 --> 00:05:46.940
Or maybe, this just might be because...

00:05:48.010 --> 00:05:56.790
<b>North Wind</b>

00:05:48.010 --> 00:05:56.790
<b>Sun</b>

00:05:48.320 --> 00:05:52.270
"Hey, why don't we have 
a test of strength?"

00:05:52.270 --> 00:05:56.800
"Which of us can take the 
jackets off the students?"

00:05:56.990 --> 00:05:57.900
All right!

00:05:57.900 --> 00:05:59.670
We're not going to lose to 
either the sun or the north wind!

00:05:59.670 --> 00:06:00.940
Let's go, Awara!

00:06:01.150 --> 00:06:02.160
Right!

00:06:02.160 --> 00:06:03.960
We won't lose to the 
north wind or the sun!

00:06:03.960 --> 00:06:05.110
Let's go, Mitsui!

00:06:07.060 --> 00:06:11.080
You should know, the wind's 
coming straight out of the west.

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:17.630
They say that pencils used for sketching

00:06:17.630 --> 00:06:20.260
should be sharpened with 
a blade, not a sharpener.

00:06:20.650 --> 00:06:23.230
The teacher said to 
always do that, if we can.

00:06:23.230 --> 00:06:24.790
If we sharpen it ourselves,

00:06:24.790 --> 00:06:28.860
we can control the thickness 
and the sharpness of the lead.

00:06:29.270 --> 00:06:33.500
But if you're clumsy like me, 
it's a bit of a challenge.

00:06:34.180 --> 00:06:35.270
I guess that's about right.

00:06:35.270 --> 00:06:37.320
Oh, Tomokane, you're quite skilled.

00:06:37.320 --> 00:06:41.790
Absolutely! Using the pencil 
until it becomes that small!

00:06:41.790 --> 00:06:42.970
What are you talking about?

00:06:42.970 --> 00:06:45.380
This is a brand new pencil 
that I just sharpened.

00:06:45.570 --> 00:06:46.410
All of these too.

00:06:47.630 --> 00:06:49.140
Could that mountain be...

00:06:49.140 --> 00:06:52.690
Tomokane, I think it might be best 
for you to use one of these...

00:06:52.690 --> 00:06:53.930
for the earth's sake.

00:06:54.260 --> 00:06:57.060
I feel like we struggled with 
this when we were first years,

00:06:57.060 --> 00:07:01.080
but you get used to it by the 
time you're a third year.

00:07:01.080 --> 00:07:04.110
Aa-san, you used to be terrible 
at sharpening pencils, remember?

00:07:04.110 --> 00:07:07.210
Seriously. Compared to before, 
you've gotten so much better.

00:07:07.210 --> 00:07:11.790
Now I'm sharpening with 
lots of things in mind.

00:07:11.790 --> 00:07:13.710
Hmmm, like what?

00:07:14.070 --> 00:07:15.710
Like how closely I can 
make the pencil shavings

00:07:15.710 --> 00:07:17.120
resemble bonito flakes.

00:07:17.120 --> 00:07:18.640
That sounds delicious.

00:07:18.640 --> 00:07:20.710
Then, how about cutting a long, thin strip?

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:25.240
Buchi-san, you've gotten much 
better at dealing with people as well.

00:07:25.870 --> 00:07:28.210
Oh yeah. Did you see this?

00:07:28.210 --> 00:07:31.130
Apparently a girl from 
our school is in it.

00:07:31.380 --> 00:07:35.440
Oh, I heard about that. 
They say she's really cute!

00:07:35.440 --> 00:07:37.360
I think she's a special day student 
in the General Studies Department...

00:07:37.360 --> 00:07:39.770
What was her name again? 
I think it was...

00:07:40.690 --> 00:07:41.980
Here! This girl!

00:07:41.980 --> 00:07:44.680
Noda-san, 17 years old. 
General Studies Senior.

00:07:44.680 --> 00:07:46.650
Doesn't she look like a model?

00:07:46.650 --> 00:07:47.710
Yeah.

00:07:47.710 --> 00:07:49.310
If she's a General 
Studies Senior,

00:07:49.310 --> 00:07:51.580
then she must be in Uozumi's class.

00:07:51.790 --> 00:07:54.350
Whoa! Aa-san, that's amazing!

00:07:54.610 --> 00:07:56.080
That's masterful skill.

00:08:04.570 --> 00:08:05.360
Hmm...?

00:08:06.860 --> 00:08:09.000
Oh, it's just more Noda-fans.

00:08:09.180 --> 00:08:10.490
Since she got into this magazine,

00:08:10.490 --> 00:08:13.070
they're even livelier 
than usual.

00:08:13.580 --> 00:08:15.000
Here. You can have this back.

00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:16.890
You know, you look

00:08:16.890 --> 00:08:18.700
even more antisocial than usual, today.

00:08:21.210 --> 00:08:23.400
I feel like I might have a headache.

00:08:23.400 --> 00:08:24.950
Why don't you go to 
the nurse's office?

00:08:24.950 --> 00:08:27.510
Oh, I'm a health committee member.

00:08:27.510 --> 00:08:29.460
Let's go to the nurse's 
office, Uozumi-kun.

00:08:29.460 --> 00:08:30.150
Huh?

00:08:30.150 --> 00:08:33.660
Wait. It'll get even 
noisier if you go.

00:08:34.140 --> 00:08:35.790
I'll be fine on my own.

00:08:35.790 --> 00:08:36.430
Really?

00:08:36.660 --> 00:08:37.830
Hey Noda!

00:08:38.040 --> 00:08:39.400
Hmm? What is it?

00:08:39.400 --> 00:08:41.950
The girl that's in this 
magazine is your sister, right?

00:08:41.950 --> 00:08:42.830
That's right.

00:08:42.830 --> 00:08:46.700
Wow. Noda-chan's sister 
is in a fashion magazine?

00:08:46.700 --> 00:08:48.150
See? Look.

00:08:48.150 --> 00:08:50.830
Oh! She sure looks sisterly.

00:08:50.830 --> 00:08:53.180
She seems to be in 
these once in a while.

00:08:53.500 --> 00:08:54.500
What's going on?

00:08:54.500 --> 00:08:55.390
Lemme see.

00:08:55.390 --> 00:08:57.170
It's Noda-chan's sister!

00:08:57.920 --> 00:08:59.650
I'm the one who found it.

00:09:01.200 --> 00:09:02.500
Excuse me.

00:09:02.500 --> 00:09:03.150
Huh?

00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:05.300
I guess the doctor's out.

00:09:06.380 --> 00:09:09.160
I guess I'll grab some 
headache medicine for now.

00:09:09.640 --> 00:09:11.510
Where do they keep the medicine anyway?

00:09:11.810 --> 00:09:15.170
If you're looking for headache medicine, 
it's the fourth shelf on the right.

00:09:15.170 --> 00:09:15.670
Huh?

00:09:16.320 --> 00:09:17.720
You're here?

00:09:17.720 --> 00:09:19.770
Yup. I usually am.

00:09:19.770 --> 00:09:22.070
What's your headache like?

00:09:22.070 --> 00:09:24.000
Like a dull pain...

00:09:24.480 --> 00:09:25.580
Then maybe this one.

00:09:26.140 --> 00:09:27.430
Two tablets per dose.

00:09:27.430 --> 00:09:28.370
All right.

00:09:28.370 --> 00:09:29.580
There's water over there.

00:09:34.170 --> 00:09:35.550
Oh, thanks.

00:09:35.550 --> 00:09:36.870
Shall I check your temperature?

00:09:36.870 --> 00:09:39.160
Oh no, I think I'm fine.

00:09:39.160 --> 00:09:40.270
Oh okay.

00:09:40.270 --> 00:09:43.150
But if it's hurting, then you 
should probably lie down...

00:09:45.530 --> 00:09:47.230
You should lie down.

00:09:49.390 --> 00:09:52.630
Noda-chan, you need to 
add salt when dyeing.

00:09:52.630 --> 00:09:55.010
Wha? Then should I get 
some from the cafeteria?

00:09:55.010 --> 00:09:56.270
<b>Salt</b>

00:09:55.520 --> 00:09:56.270
Here's some.

00:09:56.690 --> 00:09:58.280
This is such a help!

00:09:58.280 --> 00:10:01.700
Kyouju, do you carry supplies for 
a journey under your uniform?

00:10:02.420 --> 00:10:03.730
You don't need to show 
us your toothbrush.

00:10:07.200 --> 00:10:09.050
I'm feeling kind of sick.

00:10:09.250 --> 00:10:12.030
Oh! Did you eat lunch today?

00:10:12.030 --> 00:10:14.750
You said something about 
a diet the other day.

00:10:14.750 --> 00:10:16.850
No, I was doing my assignment and...

00:10:16.850 --> 00:10:18.490
Your blood sugar is probably low.

00:10:18.180 --> 00:10:19.330
<b>Ta-da</b>

00:10:20.280 --> 00:10:21.210
Take it.

00:10:21.930 --> 00:10:23.200
Huh? It's cold.

00:10:23.620 --> 00:10:26.110
Maybe I'll ask to be 
Kyouju's apprentice.

00:10:26.550 --> 00:10:29.240
We just bought them a second ago.

00:10:29.690 --> 00:10:30.230
<b>Pshk</b>

00:10:36.400 --> 00:10:41.000
<b>Flop~</b>

00:10:37.440 --> 00:10:39.360
She's drunk off of 
grape soda?!

00:10:39.360 --> 00:10:41.020
There really are people like that!

00:10:45.850 --> 00:10:47.530
Kisaragi! Stay with me.

00:10:48.210 --> 00:10:49.650
Looks like the doctor is out.

00:10:49.650 --> 00:10:51.240
I'll go check the staff room.

00:10:51.240 --> 00:10:52.420
I'll go too.

00:10:52.420 --> 00:10:53.800
Let's lie her down for now.

00:10:53.800 --> 00:10:54.430
Okay.

00:10:55.530 --> 00:10:56.530
Oh, sorry!

00:10:57.020 --> 00:10:58.080
Someone was sleeping.

00:10:58.080 --> 00:11:00.070
There's another bed, right?

00:11:00.070 --> 00:11:04.040
U-Um. I think I might be fine now.

00:11:04.040 --> 00:11:05.020
Really?

00:11:05.020 --> 00:11:06.340
Y-Yes! Somehow.

00:11:07.000 --> 00:11:08.710
Well, if you say so.

00:11:12.340 --> 00:11:13.810
Did someone come in?

00:11:14.460 --> 00:11:15.540
Hmm?

00:11:17.700 --> 00:11:19.490
I guess no one's here.

00:11:22.230 --> 00:11:24.950
In the end, I guess 
you were just really hungry.

00:11:24.950 --> 00:11:28.220
Yes. What an embarrassing story.

00:11:28.220 --> 00:11:30.600
I felt much better after 
eating some sweets.

00:11:30.880 --> 00:11:34.520
Sweets work better than 
any medicine for girls!

00:11:35.210 --> 00:11:39.120
Boooh! Luxury cruise 
ship departing! Boooh!

00:11:39.120 --> 00:11:40.100
Oh! It's a ship!

00:11:41.170 --> 00:11:42.260
There's the destroyer.

00:11:42.260 --> 00:11:43.790
Actually it was the Titanic.

00:11:43.790 --> 00:11:44.750
The Titanic?

00:11:44.960 --> 00:11:47.140
Don't play with sweets.

00:11:47.140 --> 00:11:49.550
See? You made them fly 
all over the place.

00:11:49.550 --> 00:11:52.410
Oh, but the package for these sweets...

00:11:53.890 --> 00:11:57.020
It's so thin, yet so strong.

00:11:57.020 --> 00:12:00.720
It's only slightly, but even when 
I bend or twist it... see?

00:12:00.720 --> 00:12:02.270
It springs back to shape.

00:12:02.270 --> 00:12:02.770
You're right.

00:12:02.770 --> 00:12:05.540
It was actually shape-memory Titanic.

00:12:05.540 --> 00:12:07.570
No, that doesn't make any sense at all...

00:12:07.570 --> 00:12:10.040
Geijutsuka Art Design Class

00:12:10.040 --> 00:12:15.040
Geijutsuka Art Design Class

00:12:10.680 --> 00:12:12.650
Oh, I'm a health committee member.

00:12:12.650 --> 00:12:14.700
It's Noda-chan's sister!

00:12:18.210 --> 00:12:19.890
I'm going to throw out the water.

00:12:19.890 --> 00:12:20.550
Okay.

00:12:20.550 --> 00:12:22.050
Oh! I'll come with.

00:12:24.560 --> 00:12:26.570
Man, there's no way.

00:12:26.570 --> 00:12:28.800
We'll never clean the courtyard.

00:12:28.800 --> 00:12:31.400
I never thought they were so violent.

00:12:31.600 --> 00:12:35.030
As soon as you enter with a 
broom, it's a beak attack.

00:12:35.030 --> 00:12:38.170
Even so, we can't use 
force against them.

00:12:38.530 --> 00:12:40.730
If it's about the Chicken Lords...

00:12:47.380 --> 00:12:48.880
You seem to be in trouble!

00:12:49.140 --> 00:12:49.980
Flash!

00:12:50.080 --> 00:12:51.250
Who is that?

00:12:51.250 --> 00:12:53.650
If you're in trouble, leave it to us!

00:12:54.010 --> 00:12:56.180
If you can think of it, 
I'll lead the way!

00:12:56.180 --> 00:12:57.890
I'll allow no objection, Fauvism!

00:12:58.070 --> 00:12:59.620
The color of destruction and passion,

00:12:59.620 --> 00:13:01.060
Irodorun Red!

00:13:02.070 --> 00:13:04.260
First to jut in, second to appreciate.

00:13:04.260 --> 00:13:06.060
A recognized and respected hard worker!

00:13:06.060 --> 00:13:10.600
The color of warning and spice,
 Irodorun Yellow!

00:13:10.960 --> 00:13:12.000
Sharanra~

00:13:12.390 --> 00:13:14.750
Full of charm, the sexy genius.

00:13:14.750 --> 00:13:17.620
The color of love and maidens,
 Irodorun Magenta!

00:13:18.810 --> 00:13:20.610
Um... um...

00:13:20.610 --> 00:13:23.110
Showing kindness to the earth and to people.

00:13:23.110 --> 00:13:24.520
Loves sunken hearths!

00:13:24.650 --> 00:13:26.650
The soothing color of underwater.

00:13:26.850 --> 00:13:28.480
Irodorun Cyan!

00:13:29.580 --> 00:13:30.990
Mysterious being.

00:13:30.990 --> 00:13:33.160
The black hole within the team.

00:13:33.160 --> 00:13:34.930
Neon light to the fundamentals.

00:13:34.930 --> 00:13:36.660
Irodorun Black!

00:13:37.900 --> 00:13:41.840
The visible light reflected in the eye 
is the color of tomorrow's hope!

00:13:41.840 --> 00:13:45.300
No matter how clouded, we will illuminate 
your soul and it will shine like a rainbow!

00:13:45.300 --> 00:13:48.830
We are the Color Warriors, 
Irodo Rangers!

00:13:49.470 --> 00:13:51.580
Now, then! Today, our enemy is...

00:13:51.580 --> 00:13:52.710
Flash!

00:13:52.710 --> 00:13:54.270
There you are! 
Chicken Monster!

00:13:57.800 --> 00:13:58.550
Whoa, it's huge.

00:13:59.260 --> 00:14:00.410
It's really huge.

00:14:00.410 --> 00:14:02.020
It's too big!

00:14:02.020 --> 00:14:04.950
Now now, Irodo Rangers.

00:14:04.950 --> 00:14:07.150
Can I help you with something today?

00:14:07.150 --> 00:14:08.770
Don't get in the way 
of their cleaning!

00:14:08.770 --> 00:14:11.390
Stand aside and let 
the upperclassmen clean up!

00:14:13.310 --> 00:14:16.390
We never had any intention 
of getting in the way.

00:14:16.390 --> 00:14:18.200
Go ahead and clean as you wish!

00:14:19.750 --> 00:14:20.760
Damn.

00:14:20.760 --> 00:14:21.890
How should we fight?

00:14:21.890 --> 00:14:25.380
His wording is polite but I feel like 
we're being looked down upon.

00:14:25.910 --> 00:14:26.830
How rude.

00:14:26.830 --> 00:14:28.950
I like his roundness, but...

00:14:29.280 --> 00:14:30.650
He's not cute at all.

00:14:32.520 --> 00:14:36.460
Go ahead! 
Please clean the courtyard!

00:14:36.460 --> 00:14:37.520
How irritating!

00:14:37.520 --> 00:14:39.160
Let's finish him!

00:14:40.390 --> 00:14:41.390
Go, Magenta!

00:14:41.390 --> 00:14:42.030
Roger!

00:14:45.960 --> 00:14:48.600
Bird!

00:14:51.800 --> 00:14:53.280
I wrote “Bird” on him!

00:14:51.820 --> 00:15:03.300
 Bird

00:14:53.280 --> 00:14:56.060
Lemon yellow won't stand 
out on a white chicken!

00:14:56.060 --> 00:14:58.990
What do you think you're doing? Huh?

00:15:00.660 --> 00:15:03.310
Next is... Yellow or Cyan.

00:15:03.310 --> 00:15:05.050
What's with that ambiguous command?

00:15:05.050 --> 00:15:07.460
Wha? Is it me? Me?

00:15:07.850 --> 00:15:09.100
Fine then, Yellow.

00:15:09.100 --> 00:15:11.100
Don't say “Fine then." 
It's discouraging.

00:15:11.100 --> 00:15:12.190
How careless!

00:15:14.370 --> 00:15:17.760
Perhaps I will disrupt cleaning all over the school!

00:15:18.290 --> 00:15:21.770
And I'm thinking up a great and
evil deed to create more trouble for you.

00:15:21.770 --> 00:15:24.340
All right! Combination attack! 
Here we go, Cyan!

00:15:24.340 --> 00:15:25.670
O-Okay!

00:15:28.360 --> 00:15:31.010
It's gotta be this, right?
 Masking Tape!

00:15:35.450 --> 00:15:36.970
I'm leaving the rest to you, Cyan!

00:15:36.970 --> 00:15:37.680
Okay!

00:15:37.680 --> 00:15:39.180
I'll also go with the usual...

00:15:39.180 --> 00:15:40.540
Spattering!

00:15:45.900 --> 00:15:47.900
Well, she sure works steadily.

00:15:47.900 --> 00:15:49.460
That's her good point.

00:15:51.190 --> 00:15:53.760
I tried coloring with 
dark blue this time.

00:15:53.760 --> 00:15:54.930
Hmm! Looks good!

00:15:54.930 --> 00:15:56.260
We'll wait a little to dry.

00:15:56.260 --> 00:16:00.860
All right! I'll take care of the final 
tape removal myself! Here I go!

00:16:00.860 --> 00:16:01.510
Carefully!

00:16:01.510 --> 00:16:02.870
I got it!

00:16:03.140 --> 00:16:04.840
There are bird feathers 
underneath the tape...

00:16:05.140 --> 00:16:07.210
So I'll softly and gently...

00:16:07.210 --> 00:16:08.120
rip it off!

00:16:08.120 --> 00:16:09.550
Complete!

00:16:08.160 --> 00:16:09.550
<b>Complete!</b>

00:16:09.810 --> 00:16:11.240
Yup! Looks good.

00:16:11.240 --> 00:16:12.510
We did it!

00:16:12.510 --> 00:16:13.700
And the composition?

00:16:13.700 --> 00:16:15.060
Seems fine, right?

00:16:15.060 --> 00:16:16.950
I want to fly!

00:16:24.510 --> 00:16:27.330
No! He's getting 
even more monstrous!

00:16:29.670 --> 00:16:31.980
Wow! Is this the second transformation?

00:16:31.980 --> 00:16:33.160
So stubborn.

00:16:33.160 --> 00:16:34.790
He's not cute at all!

00:16:34.790 --> 00:16:36.090
What should we do?

00:16:36.090 --> 00:16:37.090
I guess, we'll just watch.

00:16:37.090 --> 00:16:39.150
We'll just have to go with that!

00:16:39.150 --> 00:16:39.640
“That”?

00:16:39.640 --> 00:16:42.220
The only thing that can be meant by 
“that” is “that”!

00:16:42.220 --> 00:16:44.180
What do you mean by “that”?!

00:16:44.670 --> 00:16:46.580
Somebody's ginormous robot!

00:16:47.070 --> 00:16:49.750
Coloring okay! Let's paint!

00:16:50.500 --> 00:16:52.360
Where? There? Where? Here?

00:16:55.210 --> 00:16:57.000
Irodorun Brush-Missile-Gun!

00:17:11.940 --> 00:17:14.980
It's my turn now.

00:17:30.340 --> 00:17:32.400
I'm here to intrude.

00:17:32.400 --> 00:17:35.470
I'll make you understand that 
you will never defeat me.

00:17:40.230 --> 00:17:41.070
Kyouju!

00:17:41.230 --> 00:17:42.070
Masa!

00:17:44.910 --> 00:17:45.920
What do you th-

00:17:51.880 --> 00:17:53.150
What's this? 
This is bad...

00:17:58.150 --> 00:18:02.490
No, you don't understand. 
I wasn't trying to be conceited!

00:18:02.490 --> 00:18:05.000
I'll end here for today.

00:18:10.440 --> 00:18:12.940
Kyouju, what was that technique?

00:18:12.940 --> 00:18:15.200
Something very “that”-esque.

00:18:15.310 --> 00:18:16.470
<b>Oooh!</b>

00:18:18.580 --> 00:18:19.840
Amazing!

00:18:19.840 --> 00:18:21.250
Just what you'd expect 
from her, right?

00:18:26.870 --> 00:18:29.150
Huh? Is it starting to rain?

00:18:29.610 --> 00:18:31.660
You're right. We'd 
better hurry back.

00:18:32.190 --> 00:18:34.490
Damn, I should've gone with scissors.

00:18:34.490 --> 00:18:35.610
How rude!

00:18:35.610 --> 00:18:38.200
Isn't it because of that, 
that you're on a date with me?

00:18:38.200 --> 00:18:39.370
What's that supposed to mean?

00:18:39.370 --> 00:18:41.920
...said it was amazing! 
Check out the courtyard!

00:18:41.920 --> 00:18:44.700
They said there was a girl who's 
making the Chicken Lords march in a line!

00:18:44.700 --> 00:18:45.440
What!

00:18:49.440 --> 00:18:51.440
Whoa. It's really coming down.

00:18:51.620 --> 00:18:54.150
Shoot! I forgot my umbrella!

00:18:54.150 --> 00:18:54.850
Anyone else?

00:18:55.060 --> 00:18:56.130
I brought mine.

00:18:56.130 --> 00:18:57.160
I'm in the habit of not using one.

00:18:57.160 --> 00:18:58.290
I'm in the habit of 
sharing someone else's!

00:18:58.290 --> 00:18:59.790
Don't be proud about that!

00:18:59.790 --> 00:19:03.980
Oh, don't worry. I have one 
that I bought just yesterday.

00:19:05.170 --> 00:19:06.710
Nice, Kisaragi.

00:19:06.710 --> 00:19:08.130
It should fit two or three-

00:19:12.630 --> 00:19:15.390
Kisaragi-chan is putting away her 
umbrella like it never even happened!

00:19:15.390 --> 00:19:17.720
You brat! Grab her arms 
and steal that umbrella!

00:19:17.720 --> 00:19:18.400
She ran away!

00:19:18.990 --> 00:19:21.110
I wonder if it'll stop.

00:19:21.110 --> 00:19:23.990
Yes. Maybe in a little while.

00:19:38.210 --> 00:19:39.070
<b>Whap</b>

00:19:38.550 --> 00:19:39.290
Ouch!

00:19:51.480 --> 00:19:53.720
It stopped raining, huh?

00:19:54.240 --> 00:19:55.140
Yeah.

00:20:02.780 --> 00:20:04.780
I guess we didn't need 
umbrellas after all.

00:20:04.780 --> 00:20:08.280
Someday, I'll make Kisaragi open 
her umbrella with these hands!

00:20:10.350 --> 00:20:12.790
Look, look everyone! Up there!

00:20:12.790 --> 00:20:14.330
Whoa! It's a rainbow!

00:20:14.330 --> 00:20:16.730
Let's see, one, two, three...

00:20:16.730 --> 00:20:17.770
Four!

00:20:18.730 --> 00:20:21.070
You always end up checking to see if 
there are seven colors, don't you?!

00:20:21.080 --> 00:20:29.560
 Chapter 10 Diffraction Spectrum

00:20:21.780 --> 00:20:27.180
The seven colors: Red, orange, yellow, 
green, blue, indigo, purple.

00:20:27.180 --> 00:20:29.570
The spectrum of sunlight.

00:20:29.690 --> 00:20:31.260
But I heard that in western culture,

00:20:31.260 --> 00:20:33.910
there are only six colors 
in the rainbow spectrum.

00:20:33.910 --> 00:20:35.770
What? Is that true?

00:20:35.770 --> 00:20:38.350
Yup. They don't have 
indigo over there.

00:20:39.430 --> 00:20:42.730
Then, I wonder why there 
are seven colors in Japan.

00:20:42.730 --> 00:20:44.620
I wonder where the 
extra color came from.

00:20:44.620 --> 00:20:46.890
Sorry. I was the one who did it.

00:20:46.890 --> 00:20:48.580
I didn't say anything 
about it until now.

00:20:48.580 --> 00:20:49.930
You added the extra color?!

00:20:49.930 --> 00:20:51.200
Who are you?!

00:20:51.200 --> 00:20:52.170
Ahem!

00:20:52.170 --> 00:20:53.530
Again with those jokes.

00:20:53.530 --> 00:20:54.950
It's not that a color was added.

00:20:55.520 --> 00:20:57.960
Rather, when the spectrum 
was first discovered by Newton

00:20:57.960 --> 00:21:00.360
it was divided into seven colors.

00:21:00.360 --> 00:21:02.880
Um, is that the 
law of universal gravitation person?

00:21:02.880 --> 00:21:03.510
Yes.

00:21:03.680 --> 00:21:06.910
Newton said that “light 
itself does not have color,

00:21:06.910 --> 00:21:09.740
but rather it is humans 
who sense color.”

00:21:09.740 --> 00:21:10.580
Hmm.

00:21:10.580 --> 00:21:12.450
That Newton-san did?

00:21:12.450 --> 00:21:13.790
Like you've met him?

00:21:14.300 --> 00:21:15.270
 Newton

00:21:15.700 --> 00:21:16.200
Whump

00:21:16.340 --> 00:21:18.480
I wonder why apples are red?

00:21:18.480 --> 00:21:20.220
Oh of course! It must be 
because of the spectrum!

00:21:20.310 --> 00:21:20.900
Ponk!

00:21:20.750 --> 00:21:23.760
Does everything that Newton discovers 
have to come from apples?!

00:21:25.650 --> 00:21:26.390
Yes!

00:21:26.390 --> 00:21:28.940
Oh! Noda, did you figure something 
out from apples as well?

00:21:34.620 --> 00:21:37.990
From this month's new menu at 
Wa-Café, in front of the train station, right?

00:21:38.430 --> 00:21:39.860
How come you know, Masa?

00:21:39.860 --> 00:21:41.340
I want to eat it!

00:21:41.340 --> 00:21:43.020
All right. Then, how about we all go?

00:21:43.020 --> 00:21:44.480
Yahoo!

00:21:44.700 --> 00:21:45.550
Let's go!

00:21:45.550 --> 00:21:46.220
All right!

00:21:46.220 --> 00:21:47.750
Don't get overexcited and fall down.

00:21:47.750 --> 00:21:48.750
Okay!

00:21:48.750 --> 00:21:51.900
Ride the middle of the escalator 
and hold onto the railings.

00:21:50.170 --> 00:21:55.010
 For a limited time only!
Rice-Dumpling-Cinnamon-Apple-Azuki-Sweet-Bean-Crepe!

00:21:51.900 --> 00:21:53.270
Okay!

00:23:25.070 --> 00:23:40.900
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:23:25.970 --> 00:23:28.250
Something has arrived at the 
entrance to the school!

00:23:28.250 --> 00:23:29.920
Oh, it's the blood drive.

00:23:29.920 --> 00:23:30.970
Oh! I thought so!

00:23:30.970 --> 00:23:33.800
So if you donate blood, 
you're allowed to skip class, right?

00:23:33.800 --> 00:23:35.740
You can only donate 
blood if you're 16.

00:23:35.740 --> 00:23:38.970
What?! So only Namiko-san 
and Yoshikawa-chi?

00:23:36.080 --> 00:23:40.900
The Border Between Life and Death
